        "evidence": "'By the geometrization of knot complements, these are PRECISELY the torus knots (and the unknot).' The exactness claim is false.",
        "notes": "Thurston's trichotomy is torus / SATELLITE / hyperbolic, and the vanishing-simplicial-volume class is the graph-manifold class: torus knots, the unknot, AND their connected sums and iterated cables. The granny knot 3_1 # 3_1 has zero volume and is not a torus knot (torus knots are prime); nor are cables of torus knots. PROPOSED: 'these are the knots whose complements are graph manifolds \u2014 the torus knots, the unknot, and their connected sums and iterated cables'. SECOND ITEM: the fermion dictionary 'the unknot (neutrino), trefoil 3_1 (electron), cinquefoil 5_1 (tau), and the torus(p,2) family' SKIPS THE MUON, the framework's own CAL-2 proxy. That may be deliberate, since the muon is tied to the hyperbolic figure-eight 4_1 (Vol = 2.0299, not zero) and so is not a zero-volume fundamental \u2014 but then the list should say so rather than leave a gap between the electron and the tau. THIRD ITEM: the closing paragraph duplicates verbatim the corollary already given in skein-mass-from-linking-proof.md."
